5fb9e6077069f63aac8afc09090f5453ece33c0b4ab5fb79f.png)\n\nA group of $10$ high school students is surveyed about their study habits. The scatter plot above shows the relationship between the amount of time they watch TV per week and their overall math scores. What is the overall math score of the student who watches TV for $10$ hours per week?" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/500b2e9395d0af1b9ae86ce6e9b874b817690b61faad548c1fa9e33d495a5776.png)\n\nTo determine the overall math score of the student who watches TV for $10$ hours, we locate $10$ on the horizontal axis and move in the vertical direction until we find some points, as shown above.\n\nThe highlighted point has coordinates $(10,75).$ Therefore, the overall math score of the student who watches TV for $10$ hours per week is $75%.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-134087/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7f99f2aa-f977-5d6e-ae62-a826a897ba9b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-134087"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-133622"] :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our scatter plot.\n\n- Statement I is true. The scatter plot has only one dot whose vertical coordinate equals $3.5,$ namely, $(5,3.5).$ This means that only one child spends $3.5$ hours playing outdoors.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/0103370189c7156f9677ca576e2480bc99314cd312702fca3ea3e50cb4f7287a.png)\n\n- Statement II is false. The scatter plot has two dots whose horizontal coordinate equals $6,$ namely, $(6,2)$ and $(6,2.5).$ This means that there were two children of age $6$ among those surveyed.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/0a8ca9628b48e643e1aa9e9f0216148881db237c2d29054b29f4377ad182503d.png)\n\n- Statement III is false. From the scatter plot, two children spend less than $2$ hours playing outdoors. Those children are represented by the two dots below the horizontal line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/4d9709c131045f2e440204f79ad3fd8ff22707312b0e99138da558393e8b7f6d.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-134139/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "a120b98f-8d5c-5fc8-b135-d8787a810ff3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134139/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "8d321eb8-847f-5122-990d-9e51d6ce8913" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134139/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "acc5bf35-548f-546f-9760-36c31a650f6a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134139/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "6fd8381b-575b-57e1-a055-6d0b109a4637" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134139/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "c3564eea-7797-54b8-acb8-a0e7c84860fc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134139/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8969df3b-9e06-59cd-a66b-83c1ff53cb37" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-134139/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-134139/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-134139/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-134139/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-134139/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-134139/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-134139" :question/id #uuid "a5695618-d5cd-597b-aa17-57a1d31983f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-134139" :question/is-example false :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/376bd65db6b1d0a91c6013462e686ffad4d8acceee4948e61cf291d6403a12cd.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above is based on data collected from several homes in a given community. It shows the relationship between the age of a house and the number of people living in it. \n\nGiven that none of the points overlap, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- There is only one house where precisely $3$ people live.\n- Two of the houses are $16$ years old.\n- Only one house is older than $24$ years old." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our scatter plot.\n\n- Statement I is true. The scatter plot has only one dot whose vertical coordinate equals $3,$ namely, $(18,3).$ This means that there is only one house where $3$ people live.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/7a56236f0c5649a64436809b2a5e1fb8f00ed3d345cd81c571f96d579d6c19b6.png)\n\n \n\n- Statement II is false. The scatter plot has only one dot whose horizontal coordinate equals $16,$ namely, $(16,6).$ This means that only one house is $16$ years old.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/6d9a60cd10c6d7cc9f9d51d0be44c32cb688e19da988b3e84b30f0c4be32a2a8.png)\n\n- Statement III is false. From the scatter plot, two houses are more than $24$ years old, represented by the two dots to the right of the vertical line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/44b7395bb2e5ee0a71899869e6caedb949e8744adde314134f6a09e4c8f8a35d.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-134139/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "35453324-c2ff-5be4-86aa-70b3085154dc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-134139"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-134105/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "1af3cbfb-e55e-5dbf-bcd5-4591e707f871" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134105/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "295f5dec-32aa-5bb8-8e35-3b058390c4c0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134105/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "a7539b53-6f66-5afd-b011-6507ad54ce73" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134105/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "f8dc7b12-58ec-51bb-842e-1dbc73c8020c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134105/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "f8f00d4d-60fe-5e22-bdfa-72944431d9d8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134105/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bbe62272-71d7-5da3-9f2e-a686a3433481" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-134105/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-134105/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-134105/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-134105/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-134105/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-134105/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-134105" :question/id #uuid "df37bdae-6ef8-5470-898d-00206f96df51" :question/math-academy-id "q-134105" :question/is-example false :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/5768d8f90d3dd754471a69d25582eca6cdb2f4993b9b22020dc9f2038aa61954.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above summarizes data collected by a Midwestern high school showing the relationship between the number of absences in a month and the class size. \n\nGiven that none of the points overlap, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- Only one class reported a total of $6$ absences in the month.\n- Two classes have a total of $20$ students each.\n- Only one class has more than $24$ students." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our scatter plot.\n\n- Statement I is false. The scatter plot has two points whose vertical coordinate is equal to $6,$ namely, $(16,6)$ and $(20,6).$ This means that two of the classes each reported a total of 6 absences in the month.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/a62b1d5a63764b38013fdbdba9ba85a4495cd996a2d9f975dbe3d7eb89166234.png)\n\n  \n\n- Statement II is false. The scatter plot has only one dot whose horizontal coordinate equals $20,$ namely, $(20,6).$ This means that only one of the classes has a total of  $20$ students.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/3c41f2e111ef141511ec4f2faa655ddcea8f2b7e0b73bd37f0b1e142d5d60f14.png)\n\n- Statement III is true. From the scatter plot, only one class has more than $24$ students. This class is represented by the point to the right of the vertical line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/adcba37370fdac69b152a8d18ef710d5f665d9a3252376ea312808be7d08a407.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-134105/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "35453324-c2ff-5be4-86aa-70b3085154dc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-134105"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-134128/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "a94e25a0-f490-5d79-85c0-3d9885708946" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134128/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "a3faf374-11a0-5f61-8756-5636fc0485b1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134128/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "c56716ea-6860-57dd-9e78-481eec9697df" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134128/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "baf0d4cb-7b0d-513d-aa07-81d47071b083" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134128/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "3eec39ee-49b2-5750-8425-9409c11897b3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134128/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "28a0c842-a781-5698-984d-f250f5c3dd45" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-134128/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-134128/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-134128/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-134128/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-134128/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-134128/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-134128" :question/id #uuid "28e73ddb-620f-53f5-9b92-ba2b12215281" :question/math-academy-id "q-134128" :question/is-example false :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/69517e814dae28db96c64a662ce97b5fc40ea10355cb5a02561a0d12e1a3f845.png)\n\nA math teacher asked his students how many hours of sleep they had the\nnight before a test. The information he received is summarized in the scatter plot above.\n\nGiven that none of the points overlap, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- Only one student obtained a score of $90.$\n- Only one student slept for $6$ hours.\n- None of the students obtained a score lower than $75.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our scatter plot.\n\n- Statement I is true. The scatter plot has only one dot whose vertical coordinate equals $90,$ namely, $(7,90).$ This means that only one student obtained a score of $90.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/ef915015fa9c7685f45f26ee9cd2c10dfce5a4253aed22b6ea2ea57f0c3c26e2.png)\n\n    \n\n- Statement II is false. The scatter plot has two dots whose horizontal coordinate equals $6,$ namely, $(6,80)$ and $(6,85).$ This means that two students had  $6$ hours of sleep.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/3139ca71a780b76ca7355ddd119d6502f1cd390d67064db3a4a57801e33f2917.png)\n\n- Statement III is false. From the scatter plot, three students obtained a score lower than  $75.$  Those students are represented by the three dots below the horizontal line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/a675a94a9183a86d221bb2199dae38f9f55b9f91dff9868320b0b8f4d38b3fe9.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-134128/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "35453324-c2ff-5be4-86aa-70b3085154dc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-134128"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-134133"] :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our scatter plot.\n\n- Statement I is false. The scatter plot has two dots whose vertical coordinate equals $9.5,$ namely, $(180,9.5)$ and $(195,9.5).$ This means that two players have a shoe size of  $9\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/c2058bf02025ff359b509db01022c5d2e956d67243094a33692b90d6f1c2eac8.png)\n\n \n\n- Statement II is true. The scatter plot has only one dot whose horizontal coordinate equals $195,$ namely, $(195,\\,9.5).$ This means that only one of the players has a height of $195\\,\\text{cm}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/b8b4364dc5de11eed12840bc644b1392b36160adfdf739b96f282c2367d999fa.png)\n\n \n\n- Statement III is false. According to the scatter diagram, three players have a height greater than  $185\\,\\text{cm},$ represented by the three dots to the right of the vertical line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/aaf6d496c56c3cdc5a47e1c09e7640d7a3caa05446a75b705c042a56c116cb98.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
